From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FoAKTEE <hw609@cantab.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 14:17:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] fix(native-coeffs): take K1/K2 -> 1 in rho_Q_thermal
 when K2 underflows

- change: rho_Q_thermal uses k_ratio = K1/K2 when K2(1/Theta_e) > 0 and 1 otherwise, the guard rho_V_thermal already applies to K0/K2; the cold limit of both ratios is 1 (K1/K2 = 1 - 3/(2x) + ... at x = 1/Theta_e = 705 is 0.998)
- verify: native_cold 0 of 110808 values non-finite (7353 before); the R03 coefficient table is byte-identical (its grid starts at Theta_e = 10^-2.5)
- caveat: before this change a sample with Theta_e < 1.4e-3 inside the model cuts turned the whole pixel blank (Iinv_pol = NaN clears POLARIZATION_ACTIVE and the pixel reads out zero)
---
 src/pol_emission.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pol_emission.c b/src/pol_emission.c
index 712595f..58d480f 100755
--- a/src/pol_emission.c
+++ b/src/pol_emission.c
@@ -127,10 +127,14 @@ double rho_Q_thermal(double theta_e, double n_e, double nu, double B,
     double Xe = theta_e * sqrt(sqrt(2.) * sin(theta_B) *
                                (1.e3 * omega0 / 2. / M_PI / nu));
     double Thetaer = 1. / theta_e;
+    // K1/K2 -> 1 for cold electrons; GSL K_n underflows to 0 beyond
+    // 1/Theta_e ~ 705 (guarded as the K0/K2 ratio of rho_V_thermal)
+    double k2 = bessel_appr(2, Thetaer);
+    double k_ratio = (k2 > 0) ? bessel_appr(1, Thetaer) / k2 : 1;
 
     return 2. * M_PI * nu / 2. / SPEED_OF_LIGHT * wp2 * omega0 * omega0 /
            pow(2. * M_PI * nu, 4.) * f_m(Xe) *
-           (bessel_appr(1, Thetaer) / bessel_appr(2, Thetaer) + 6. * theta_e) *
+           (k_ratio + 6. * theta_e) *
            sin(theta_B) * sin(theta_B);
 }
 
